  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{lcc} <br />& & \\text { No. of unpaired } \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\\\<br>\\text {(A) } & \\mathrm{O}_2 & 2 \\\\<br>\\text { (B) } & \\mathrm{N}_2 & 0 \\\\<br>\\text { (C) } & \\mathrm{F}_2 & 0 \\\\<br>\\text { (D) } & \\mathrm{S}_2 & 2 \\\\<br>\\text { (E) } & \\mathrm{Cl}_2 & 0<br />\\end{array}$<br />If species contain unpaired electron than it is paramagnetic.<br />So A \\& D are paramagnetic.",
    "image": null
